# Cloudflare Pages redirects. First match wins.
#
# Purpose: carry every URL Google already has indexed on the old site over to
# the new one with a 301, so ranking signals transfer instead of hitting a 404.

# --- Apex to www -----------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: this line does not work and is kept only to document the intent.
# Cloudflare Pages matches _redirects on the PATH; it does not switch on the
# request hostname, so an apex request never matches and both hosts answer
# 200. The working fix is a zone-level Single Redirect in the Cloudflare
# dashboard (Rules > Redirect Rules): when hostname equals fastexmedia.com,
# 301 to https://www.fastexmedia.com plus the path. Until that exists the
# canonical tag is the only thing keeping the two hosts from splitting.
https://fastexmedia.com/*  https://www.fastexmedia.com/:splat  301

# --- Old blog ---------------------------------------------------------------
